 0382           ; /**************************************************************************
 0382           ; DOES:    Initializes the next available filter                    
 0382           ; RETURNS: 0 for failed init, 1 for successful init
 0382           ;  
 0382           ; This function replaces the original function that just
 0382           ; set up to 8 filters, requiring a match of all bits.
 0382           ; This function can be called as previously with just
 0382           ; the CANID argument and it will function as it previously
 0382           ; was intended.
 0382           ;  
 0382           ; This function keeps track of all filters that have been set.
 0382           ; If the address (last 7 bits in CANID as defined by 'bin'
 0382           ; after applying the mask to the CANID) in a given CANID corresponds
